rita-docs: Quick thread 1 1 I updated the "metering and dashboards" doc to add an example CSV export for finance and a short note about attribution across regions. Adding here for visibility.
noah-eng: CSV example is good. Can you show expected header names? finance always asks for exact column names.
rita-docs: Yup. Example header: date, account_id, plan_slug, model_family_id, tokens, charged_tokens, overage_amount_usd, region, capacity
greta-product: For region attribution, note that some customers route to eu nodes for data residency. Add a toggle note that billing uses the account's billing_region by default, unless `force_region` set.
rita-docs: Added a paragraph: "Billing attribution uses account.billing_region by default; for customers with forced routing, region will be set on the event as request_region."
noah-eng: Also added a tiny JS snippet to compute summarized per-account monthly totals from CSV for quick verification.
noah-eng: ```js
// aggregate csv rows (assumes parsed into objects)
function summarize(rows) {
  const m = new Map();
  rows.forEach(r => {
    const key = r.account_id + '|' + r.plan_slug + '|' + r.region;
    const cur = m.get(key) || 0;
    m.set(key, cur + Number(r.overage_amount_usd || 0));
  });
  return Array.from(m.entries()).map(([k,v]) => ({key:k, amount:v}));
}
```
rita-docs: FYI I also clarified rate-limit vs quota language: rate-limit is per-second request throttling, quota is monthly token cap. Small wording change.
greta-product: Can we add a short FAQ entry: "Why does my dashboard show different totals than billing exports?" With bullet points: sampling, delayed exports, and region attribution.
rita-docs: Added FAQ. Also switched a screenshot to use `account_id` filter and included a short blurb about linking to billing exports for audit.
